<title>USA: GM has 5,911 U.S. employees idled by strike. [CORRECTED 21:58 GMT]</title>
<headline>GM has 5,911 U.S. employees idled by strike. [CORRECTED 21:58 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>WARREN, Mich. 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>General Motors Corp said as of 1600 EDT, 5,911 of its U.S. employees have been idled as a result of the Canadian Auto Workers strike that began October 3.</p>
<p>(Company corrects number of employees in headline, 1st and 2nd paras).</p>
<p>GM said the affected employees include 1,661 from its Delphi Automotive Systems parts and components division, which is based in Pontiac, Mich.</p>
<p>The company said its next update on the effects of the strike in Canada will be made Tuesday morning at 1100 EDT.</p>
<p>-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787</p>
